vas:Canopy_Height_Model a vas:Vegetation_Property,
                          <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Soil_Property>,
                          <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual>;
                        rdfs:comment """Canopy Height Model (CHM)
The CHM is a derived LiDAR product that represents vegetation height above ground, computed as the difference between the DSM and the DTM:

CHM = DSM − DTM

It is delivered as a raster map in meters (m)."""@en;
                        rdfs:label "CHM"@en;
                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/isObservedBy> vas:CHM_UAV_LiDAR_Sensor_1.
